</section>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Additional Case Study: Why ACT Improves General Reasoning</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the main text (<a href="#S4.F4" title="In 4.4 Generalization to General Reasoning Benchmarks ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Agentic Critical Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), we showed self-verification behavior observed in ACT on GPQA-Diamond. Here we provide additional case studies analyzing IL’s <em id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">reasoning collapse</em> on general reasoning benchmarks, based on reasoning traces produced by ACT and IL (Qwen3-8B) on GPQA-Diamond and MATH-500.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>IL Causes Reasoning Collapse</h3>

<div id="A3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">IL on agentic data fine-tunes the model on short, action-heavy expert trajectories that contain minimal extended reasoning. By imitating these behavioral patterns, the model suffers catastrophic forgetting of its deep reasoning capabilities: the chain-of-thought reasoning capacity that the original model possesses is overwritten by the short-sequence, action-centric distribution of agentic data. We term this <em id="A3.SS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">reasoning collapse</em>, which explains the sharp drop in GPQA-Diamond performance observed in <a href="#S4.T3" title="In 4.4 Generalization to General Reasoning Benchmarks ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Agentic Critical Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">table</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. Reasoning collapse manifests in two characteristic ways.</p>
</div>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Unfocused meandering.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Even when the IL model does produce reasoning traces, the quality of reasoning degrades significantly. <a href="#A3.F12" title="In Unfocused meandering. ‣ C.1 IL Causes Reasoning Collapse ‣ Appendix C Additional Case Study: Why ACT Improves General Reasoning ‣ Agentic Critical Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> shows a high-energy physics problem (GPQA #7) about gamma-ray annihilation with CMB photons. ACT produces a focused 10,669-character derivation that methodically sets up the threshold energy condition and arrives at the correct answer. The IL model, by contrast, generates a 37,924-character trace, 3.5<math id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> longer, yet wanders through vague recollections and contradictory estimates, ultimately conceding “given the time I’ve spent and the lack of progress” before guessing incorrectly. The reasoning capacity has not disappeared entirely but has become diffuse and ineffective.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F12" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F12.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="98.57" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 700.39 98.57" width="700.39"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,98.57) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000080;" fill="#000080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.57 L 0 74.56 C 0 79.29 3.84 83.12 8.57 83.12 L 691.83 83.12 C 696.56 83.12 700.39 79.29 700.39 74.56 L 700.39 8.57 C 700.39 3.84 696.56 0 691.83 0 L 8.57 0 C 3.84 0 0 3.84 0 8.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F0F8FF;" fill="#F0F8FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 8.57 L 0.69 74.56 C 0.69 78.9 4.22 82.43 8.57 82.43 L 691.83 82.43 C 696.18 82.43 699.7 78.9 699.7 74.56 L 699.7 8.57 C 699.7 4.22 696.18 0.69 691.83 0.69 L 8.57 0.69 C 4.22 0.69 0.69 4.22 0.69 8.57 Z"></path></g><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.81 73.28)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_nestedsvg" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000080;" fill="#000080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.51 L 0 19.78 C 0 22.82 2.47 25.29 5.51 25.29 L 471.74 25.29 C 474.78 25.29 477.25 22.82 477.25 19.78 L 477.25 5.51 C 477.25 2.47 474.78 0 471.74 0 L 5.51 0 C 2.47 0 0 2.47 0 5.51 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000080;" fill="#000080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.57 5.51 L 1.57 19.78 C 1.57 21.95 3.34 23.72 5.51 23.72 L 471.74 23.72 C 473.91 23.72 475.68 21.95 475.68 19.78 L 475.68 5.51 C 475.68 3.34 473.91 1.57 471.74 1.57 L 5.51 1.57 C 3.34 1.57 1.57 3.34 1.57 5.51 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.39 9.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:28.34em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="450.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F12.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">GPQA-Diamond #7: Gamma-Ray CMB Annihilation Threshold</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 14.53 17.91)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:52.46em;--ltx-fo-height:3.03em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="44.28" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 41.86)" width="725.9"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F12.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:52.46em;">
<span id="A3.F12.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F12.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The universe is filled with the Cosmic Microwave Background. Consider the annihilation of high-energy <math id="A3.F12.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-rays with a CMB photon into electron-positron pairs, i.e., <math id="A3.F12.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\gamma\rightarrow e^{+}e^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\gamma\rightarrow e^{+}e^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. Find the energy of <math id="A3.F12.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma</annotation></semantics></math>-rays whose lifetimes are limited by this process. The average energy of a CMB photon is <math id="A3.F12.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{-3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{-3}</annotation></semantics></math> eV.</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A3.F12.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;">
            
<div id="A3.F12.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F12.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="293.53" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 229.14 293.53" width="229.14"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,293.53) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.57 L 0 267.98 C 0 272.71 3.84 276.55 8.57 276.55 L 220.57 276.55 C 225.3 276.55 229.14 272.71 229.14 267.98 L 229.14 8.57 C 229.14 3.84 225.3 0 220.57 0 L 8.57 0 C 3.84 0 0 3.84 0 8.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F0FFF0;" fill="#F0FFF0" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 8.57 L 0.69 267.98 C 0.69 272.33 4.22 275.86 8.57 275.86 L 220.57 275.86 C 224.92 275.86 228.45 272.33 228.45 267.98 L 228.45 8.57 C 228.45 4.22 224.92 0.69 220.57 0.69 L 8.57 0.69 C 4.22 0.69 0.69 4.22 0.69 8.57 Z"></path></g><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.81 266.7)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_nestedsvg" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.51 L 0 21.32 C 0 24.36 2.47 26.83 5.51 26.83 L 263.29 26.83 C 266.34 26.83 268.8 24.36 268.8 21.32 L 268.8 5.51 C 268.8 2.47 266.34 0 263.29 0 L 5.51 0 C 2.47 0 0 2.47 0 5.51 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.57 5.51 L 1.57 21.32 C 1.57 23.49 3.34 25.25 5.51 25.25 L 263.29 25.25 C 265.47 25.25 267.23 23.49 267.23 21.32 L 267.23 5.51 C 267.23 3.34 265.47 1.57 263.29 1.57 L 5.51 1.57 C 3.34 1.57 1.57 3.34 1.57 5.51 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.39 9.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.32em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="243.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">ACT Reasoning Trace (Correct ✓)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 14.53 18.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.63em;--ltx-fo-height:16.95em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="237.71" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 234.59)" width="216.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:15.63em;">
<span id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">For <math id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\gamma\gamma\to e^{+}e^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\gamma\gamma\to e^{+}e^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>, the total energy must be at least <math id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2m_{e}c^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2m_{e}c^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a head-on collision, the threshold condition is <math id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\gamma}\cdot E_{\text{CMB}}\geq(m_{e}c^{2})^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000">CMB</mtext></msub></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">m</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">c</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\gamma}\cdot E_{\text{CMB}}\geq(m_{e}c^{2})^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. […] So <math id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{\gamma}\geq(0.511\text{ MeV})^{2}/(10^{-3}\text{ eV})=2.61\times 10^{14}\text{ eV}\approx 2.6\times 10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">E</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">γ</mi></msub><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0.511</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000"> MeV</mtext></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000"> eV</mtext></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2.61</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">14</mn></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" class="ltx_mathvariant_italic" mathcolor="#000000"> eV</mtext></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≈</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2.6</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{\gamma}\geq(0.511\text{ MeV})^{2}/(10^{-3}\text{ eV})=2.61\times 10^{14}\text{ eV}\approx 2.6\times 10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> GeV. The gamma rays with energy just above the threshold would have their lifetimes limited by this process. Therefore, the answer is the threshold energy.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer: C (<math id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2.6\times 10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2.6</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2.6\times 10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> GeV)<span id="A3.F12.p1.pic1.2.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> ✓ (10,669 chars)</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A3.F12.4" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;">
            
<div id="A3.F12.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F12.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="358.78" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 229.14 358.78" width="229.14"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,358.78) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#DC143C;" fill="#DC143C" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.57 L 0 333.22 C 0 337.96 3.84 341.79 8.57 341.79 L 220.57 341.79 C 225.3 341.79 229.14 337.96 229.14 333.22 L 229.14 8.57 C 229.14 3.84 225.3 0 220.57 0 L 8.57 0 C 3.84 0 0 3.84 0 8.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF0F5;" fill="#FFF0F5" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 8.57 L 0.69 333.22 C 0.69 337.57 4.22 341.1 8.57 341.1 L 220.57 341.1 C 224.92 341.1 228.45 337.57 228.45 333.22 L 228.45 8.57 C 228.45 4.22 224.92 0.69 220.57 0.69 L 8.57 0.69 C 4.22 0.69 0.69 4.22 0.69 8.57 Z"></path></g><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.81 331.95)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_nestedsvg" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#DC143C;" fill="#DC143C" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.51 L 0 21.32 C 0 24.36 2.47 26.83 5.51 26.83 L 237.3 26.83 C 240.34 26.83 242.81 24.36 242.81 21.32 L 242.81 5.51 C 242.81 2.47 240.34 0 237.3 0 L 5.51 0 C 2.47 0 0 2.47 0 5.51 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#DC143C;" fill="#DC143C" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.57 5.51 L 1.57 21.32 C 1.57 23.49 3.34 25.25 5.51 25.25 L 237.3 25.25 C 239.47 25.25 241.24 23.49 241.24 21.32 L 241.24 5.51 C 241.24 3.34 239.47 1.57 237.3 1.57 L 5.51 1.57 C 3.34 1.57 1.57 3.34 1.57 5.51 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.39 9.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:13.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="207.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">IL Reasoning Trace (Wrong <math id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 14.53 18.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.63em;--ltx-fo-height:21.67em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="302.95" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 299.84)" width="216.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:15.63em;">
<span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[…after 37,924 characters of unfocused derivation…]</span></span>
<span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">However, I recall that the energy at which gamma rays can interact with CMB photons to produce <math id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e^{+}e^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">e</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{+}e^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> pairs is approximately <math id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="10^{4}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">10^{4}</annotation></semantics></math> GeV. […] Given that, the answer is likely option B or C. But I’m not certain. […]</span></span>
<span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given the time I’ve spent and the lack of progress, I’ll go with option B: <math id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.8\times 10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.8</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.8\times 10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> GeV.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer: B (<math id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.8\times 10^{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1.8</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">10</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.8\times 10^{5}</annotation></semantics></math> GeV)<span id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A3.F12.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>  (37,924 chars)</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F12.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 12</span>: </span><span id="A3.F12.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reasoning collapse: unfocused meandering. On a high-energy physics threshold problem, ACT produces a focused derivation (10K chars), while IL generates 3.5<math id="A3.F12.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math> more text (38K chars) yet wanders through vague recollections and contradictory estimates, ultimately guessing incorrectly.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Algebraic death loops.</h4>

<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On MATH-500 problems requiring sustained mathematical derivation, the IL model enters repetitive algebraic loops, producing traces exceeding 80,000 characters without reaching a correct conclusion. <a href="#A3.F13" title="In Algebraic death loops. ‣ C.1 IL Causes Reasoning Collapse ‣ Appendix C Additional Case Study: Why ACT Improves General Reasoning ‣ Agentic Critical Training" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figure</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> shows a probability problem (MATH-500 #445): ACT recognizes the geometric structure and cleanly derives the answer, while the IL model enters a prolonged algebraic spiral, repeatedly second-guesses itself, and ultimately produces an incorrect answer.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A3.F13" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F13.pic1" class="ltx_picture ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel" height="82.66" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 700.39 82.66" width="700.39"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,82.66) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000080;" fill="#000080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.57 L 0 58.64 C 0 63.37 3.84 67.21 8.57 67.21 L 691.83 67.21 C 696.56 67.21 700.39 63.37 700.39 58.64 L 700.39 8.57 C 700.39 3.84 696.56 0 691.83 0 L 8.57 0 C 3.84 0 0 3.84 0 8.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F0F8FF;" fill="#F0F8FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 8.57 L 0.69 58.64 C 0.69 62.99 4.22 66.52 8.57 66.52 L 691.83 66.52 C 696.18 66.52 699.7 62.99 699.7 58.64 L 699.7 8.57 C 699.7 4.22 696.18 0.69 691.83 0.69 L 8.57 0.69 C 4.22 0.69 0.69 4.22 0.69 8.57 Z"></path></g><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.81 57.37)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_nestedsvg" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000080;" fill="#000080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.51 L 0 19.78 C 0 22.82 2.47 25.29 5.51 25.29 L 304.17 25.29 C 307.21 25.29 309.68 22.82 309.68 19.78 L 309.68 5.51 C 309.68 2.47 307.21 0 304.17 0 L 5.51 0 C 2.47 0 0 2.47 0 5.51 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000080;" fill="#000080" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.57 5.51 L 1.57 19.78 C 1.57 21.95 3.34 23.72 5.51 23.72 L 304.17 23.72 C 306.34 23.72 308.1 21.95 308.1 19.78 L 308.1 5.51 C 308.1 3.34 306.34 1.57 304.17 1.57 L 5.51 1.57 C 3.34 1.57 1.57 3.34 1.57 5.51 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.39 9.19)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:17.89em;--ltx-fo-height:0.6em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.17em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="12.3" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 9.61)" width="284.68"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F13.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">MATH-500 #445: Rectangle Probability</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 14.53 17.91)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:52.46em;--ltx-fo-height:1.88em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.18em;font-size:10pt;" height="28.37" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 25.94)" width="725.9"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F13.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:52.46em;">
<span id="A3.F13.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F13.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Rectangle <math id="A3.F13.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD</annotation></semantics></math> has center <math id="A3.F13.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A3.F13.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="AB/AD=k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">AB/AD=k</annotation></semantics></math>. A point is randomly chosen from the interior of <math id="A3.F13.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="ABCD" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">A</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">B</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">C</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">D</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">ABCD</annotation></semantics></math>. What is the probability that it is closer to <math id="A3.F13.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> than to any of the four vertices?</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A3.F13.3" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;">
            
<div id="A3.F13.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F13.p1.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="324.53" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 229.14 324.53" width="229.14"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,324.53) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.57 L 0 298.98 C 0 303.71 3.84 307.54 8.57 307.54 L 220.57 307.54 C 225.3 307.54 229.14 303.71 229.14 298.98 L 229.14 8.57 C 229.14 3.84 225.3 0 220.57 0 L 8.57 0 C 3.84 0 0 3.84 0 8.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F0FFF0;" fill="#F0FFF0" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 8.57 L 0.69 298.98 C 0.69 303.33 4.22 306.85 8.57 306.85 L 220.57 306.85 C 224.92 306.85 228.45 303.33 228.45 298.98 L 228.45 8.57 C 228.45 4.22 224.92 0.69 220.57 0.69 L 8.57 0.69 C 4.22 0.69 0.69 4.22 0.69 8.57 Z"></path></g><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.81 297.7)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_nestedsvg" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.51 L 0 21.32 C 0 24.36 2.47 26.83 5.51 26.83 L 263.29 26.83 C 266.34 26.83 268.8 24.36 268.8 21.32 L 268.8 5.51 C 268.8 2.47 266.34 0 263.29 0 L 5.51 0 C 2.47 0 0 2.47 0 5.51 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#228B22;" fill="#228B22" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.57 5.51 L 1.57 21.32 C 1.57 23.49 3.34 25.25 5.51 25.25 L 263.29 25.25 C 265.47 25.25 267.23 23.49 267.23 21.32 L 267.23 5.51 C 267.23 3.34 265.47 1.57 263.29 1.57 L 5.51 1.57 C 3.34 1.57 1.57 3.34 1.57 5.51 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.39 9.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.32em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="243.8"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">ACT Reasoning Trace (Correct ✓)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 14.53 18.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.63em;--ltx-fo-height:19.19em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="268.7" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 265.59)" width="216.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:15.63em;">
<span id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">The set of points closer to <math id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> than to any vertex is the intersection of the four half-planes defined by the perpendicular bisectors between <math id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="O" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">O</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">O</annotation></semantics></math> and each vertex. These bisectors form a rectangle rotated by <math id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="45^{\circ}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">45</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">∘</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">45^{\circ}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose area is half of the original rectangle. Therefore, the probability is <math id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math> regardless of <math id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>. […]</span></span>
<span id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">I’ve verified for <math id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> (square case) and general <math id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>: all methods confirm that the probability is <math id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer: <math id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.F13.p1.pic1.2.3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> ✓ (42,641 chars of reasoning)</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_2">
<div id="A3.F13.4" class="ltx_logical-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_minipage ltx_align_center ltx_align_top" style="width:165.6pt;">
            
<div id="A3.F13.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent"><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="A3.F13.p2.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="391.99" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 229.14 391.99" width="229.14"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,391.99) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#DC143C;" fill="#DC143C" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 8.57 L 0 366.43 C 0 371.16 3.84 375 8.57 375 L 220.57 375 C 225.3 375 229.14 371.16 229.14 366.43 L 229.14 8.57 C 229.14 3.84 225.3 0 220.57 0 L 8.57 0 C 3.84 0 0 3.84 0 8.57 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#FFF0F5;" fill="#FFF0F5" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0.69 8.57 L 0.69 366.43 C 0.69 370.78 4.22 374.31 8.57 374.31 L 220.57 374.31 C 224.92 374.31 228.45 370.78 228.45 366.43 L 228.45 8.57 C 228.45 4.22 224.92 0.69 220.57 0.69 L 8.57 0.69 C 4.22 0.69 0.69 4.22 0.69 8.57 Z"></path></g><g transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 11.81 365.16)"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" class="ltx_nestedsvg" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="matrix(1 0 0 1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#DC143C;" fill="#DC143C" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.51 L 0 21.32 C 0 24.36 2.47 26.83 5.51 26.83 L 237.3 26.83 C 240.34 26.83 242.81 24.36 242.81 21.32 L 242.81 5.51 C 242.81 2.47 240.34 0 237.3 0 L 5.51 0 C 2.47 0 0 2.47 0 5.51 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#DC143C;" fill="#DC143C" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.57 5.51 L 1.57 21.32 C 1.57 23.49 3.34 25.25 5.51 25.25 L 237.3 25.25 C 239.47 25.25 241.24 23.49 241.24 21.32 L 241.24 5.51 C 241.24 3.34 239.47 1.57 237.3 1.57 L 5.51 1.57 C 3.34 1.57 1.57 3.34 1.57 5.51 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 13.39 9.96)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:13.07em;--ltx-fo-height:0.65em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.22em;font-size:11.5pt;" height="13.84" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 10.38)" width="207.93"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content"><span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;">IL Reasoning Trace (Wrong <math id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FFFFFF;" mathcolor="#FFFFFF">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>)</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 14.53 18.6)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:15.63em;--ltx-fo-height:24.07em;--ltx-fo-depth:0.23em;font-size:10pt;" height="336.16" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 333.05)" width="216.28"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:15.63em;">
<span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.2.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">[…after 80,000+ characters of algebraic manipulation…]</span></span>
<span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given that I’m stuck, I’ll refer back to the initial correct calculation for <math id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math>, which gave the area as 2, and the probability as <math id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>. For general <math id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math>, if the area is <math id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(k^{2}+1)^{2}/(2k)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(k^{2}+1)^{2}/(2k)</annotation></semantics></math> when it is inside the rectangle, but for <math id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k&lt;1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k&lt;1</annotation></semantics></math>, it is clipped. However, I cannot proceed further.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.2.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.2.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Given the time I’ve spent, I will conclude that the probability is <math id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-k^{2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-k^{2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></span>
<span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.2.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.2.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold" style="font-size:90%;--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Answer: <math id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{1-k^{2}}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">1</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><msup><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">k</mi><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></msup></mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{1-k^{2}}{2}</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.2.4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_medium"> <math id="A3.F13.p2.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\times" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">×</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\times</annotation></semantics></math>  (80,918 chars of reasoning)</span></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</div>
          
</div></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A3.F13.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 13</span>: </span><span id="A3.F13.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Reasoning collapse: algebraic death loop. On a probability problem, ACT cleanly identifies the geometric structure, while IL generates over 80,000 characters of circular algebraic manipulation before giving up with an incorrect answer. The IL model correctly solves the <math id="A3.F13.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k=1</annotation></semantics></math> special case early on but cannot generalize, endlessly rederiving and contradicting its own intermediate results.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<div id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">ACT avoids reasoning collapse because it optimizes for outcome correctness via RL rather than imitating behavioral patterns. Since the RL training signal rewards correct critical judgments regardless of response format or length, ACT not only acquires agentic skills but also fully preserves and even strengthens the original model’s deep reasoning capacity, compared to IL, which tends to overwrite general reasoning capabilities with domain-specific action patterns through supervised fine-tuning on short, action-centric sequences.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
